/dross
/dist
/reports
*.test
*.out
.DS_Store
STATUS.md
Brief.md
docs/dross.pdf

# dross handoff — local working memory, not tracked
.dross/handoff.md

# dross machine-local values (quick_base) — deliberately untracked: a value
# stored in tracked state would be dragged forward into every later tree by the
# squash. Staying out of history is the whole point.
.dross/local.toml

# dross machine-local position + version state — deliberately untracked: no
# ordinary commit carries a copy, so nothing can replay one over the live file.
# (On refs cut before this line landed, dross itself refuses the switch — git
# overwrites an *ignored* file without complaint.) Locked state_tracking.
.dross/state.json

# dross memory-advisor state — the turn cache, and the memory-dir snapshot taken
# before each applied prune. Machine-local: it mirrors this machine's
# ~/.claude, and a snapshot is a copy of private memory.
.dross/memory/

# dross security run artifacts — local audit output; never pre-disclose on a public repo
.dross/security/

# dross quality run artifacts — local audit output; the committed record is the remediation spec
.dross/quality/

# dross tech-debt run artifacts — local scan output; state.toml is the durable signal, run dirs are prunable
.dross/techdebt/

# dross reap ledger — machine-local record of one machine's writes to one
# tracker, deliberately untracked: a tracked ledger dirties the tree on every
# `issue reap --apply`, rides ship's clean-tree auto-commit into the phase
# branch, and drags a stale undo target through the squash into every later tree.
.dross/reap-log.json
